WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.078
- What do you remember
about the first time

00:00:01.078 --> 00:00:03.410
you were, like, ever on
stage, like in a musical?

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:04.273
- Oh, I, um-

00:00:04.273 --> 00:00:05.106
- [Kelly] Like your favorite one.

00:00:05.106 --> 00:00:08.680
- I had the most amazing
dosage of musical theater

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.770
at a young age because I had an amazing

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.836
elementary school music
teacher, Barbara Ames,

00:00:12.836 --> 00:00:14.036
shout out to Barbara Ames.

00:00:14.036 --> 00:00:14.869
- Get it, Barbara Ames.

00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:16.750
(audience cheers)

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.210
- She's actually in "Tick, Tick... Boom!"

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:19.487
I put her in the movie.

00:00:19.487 --> 00:00:20.320
- [Kelly] Oh, I love that!

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.692
- And she plays Jonathan
Larson's music teacher

00:00:21.692 --> 00:00:22.807
(chuckles) in the movie.

00:00:22.807 --> 00:00:23.700
- I love that.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.570
- I had to, I had to.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:25.533
- I know, but that's so great,

00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:26.895
like a little nugget so
everybody knows that,

00:00:26.895 --> 00:00:28.650
like while watching it, that's so cool.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.880
- Yeah, and so she would do something

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:31.920
called the sixth grade play,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.405
she would music direct and
direct the sixth grade play,

00:00:34.405 --> 00:00:37.040
and when I was in kindergarten
it was "West Side Story",

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.170
and the whole school watched it,

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.200
and when I was in first grade
it was "Fiddler on the Roof"

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.630
and so by the time you're in fifth grade,

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.340
you're like, "What's our
sixth grade play gonna be?"

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.173
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh.

00:00:45.173 --> 00:00:47.100
- And by the time we got to sixth grade

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.590
they ran out of age appropriate musicals

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.320
for 12 year olds.
- Ah.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.930
- So we did a very unauthorized,

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.139
previous six years worth of musicals,

00:00:55.139 --> 00:00:57.300
like 20 minute versions.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.539
So, when I was 12 years old-

00:00:58.539 --> 00:00:59.720
- What, did you just pick the best songs?

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.160
- We just, yeah, they did like, yeah,

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.060
they just picked the best songs

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.630
and were like, here's
a 20 minute "Fiddler",

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.618
here's a 20 minute "West Side"-

00:01:04.618 --> 00:01:05.451
- Like a variety show of
musicals, I love this.

00:01:05.451 --> 00:01:07.680
- It was four hours long, my poor parents.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.907
- Oh, my God, all those
parents hated all of you.

00:01:09.907 --> 00:01:10.890
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.830
- Hated us, on our wooden
chairs in our auditorium.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.805
But I played a farmer in
"Oklahoma", Captain Hook,

00:01:17.805 --> 00:01:19.536
Bernardo in "West Side Story".

00:01:19.536 --> 00:01:20.369
- [Kelly] What?

00:01:20.369 --> 00:01:22.517
And (indistinct) back up in "The Wiz".

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.100
And, who else, a son in "Fiddler",

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.770
it was like, just the most
amazing experience of my life.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.020
- [Kelly] What a boot camp.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.250
- When you're 12 and you play Conrad Burty

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.284
and you sing and all the girls and boys

00:01:36.284 --> 00:01:38.370
have to faint when you sing,

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.677
I was like, "I'm doing this."

00:01:39.677 --> 00:01:42.237
- "I'm amazing."
- For the rest of my life.

00:01:42.237 --> 00:01:43.180
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.186
- That's it, I'm done.

00:01:44.186 --> 00:01:45.717
- I love that.
- Yeah.

00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:47.520
- That's a lot to like, ask,

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.590
that's a high bar to ask of sixth graders.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.190
I like her, Barbara.
- I don't remember

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:52.630
any math from sixth grade,

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.230
I remember the sixth grade play.

